{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-334603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-2xy,\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nThe trapezoidal method is applied with step size $Δx=3.$ Find the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the current values $x$ and $y,$ and the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-2xy+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-2{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-2xy)-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-2xy)-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-2xy+\\frac{2}{3}y)-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-2xy+\\frac{2}{3}y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-2xy+\\frac{2}{3}y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-6xy+2y}{2+6{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-334603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-4xy+2y}{2+6{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-6xy+2y}{1+6{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-6xy+2y}{2+6{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-6xy+y}{2+6{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-6xy+2y}{2+6{x}_{\\text{new}}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}}+1)-6xy+2y}{2+6{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-333386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}-3xy,\\,y(-2)=3\n$$\n\nThe trapezoidal method is applied with step size $Δx=1.$ Find the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the current values $x$ and $y,$ and the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-333386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-3xy+({e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy)-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy)-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy+2y)-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy+2y) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}(2+3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy+2y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy+2y}{2+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-333386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-333386" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-333386" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+2y}{2-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy+2y}{2+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy+y}{1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy-2y}{2-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-333386" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3xy+2y}{2+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-x+3y,\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nThe trapezoidal method is applied with step size $Δx=1.$ Find the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the current values $x$ and $y,$ and the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x+3y+(-{x}_{\\text{new}}+3{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y)+\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y)+\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+5y)+\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+5y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-334595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-3y"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-4y"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{\\text{new}}=x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{2x}+{x}^{2}y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nThe trapezoidal method is applied with step size $Δx=2.$ Find the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the current values $x$ and $y,$ and the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2x}+{x}^{2}y+({e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{x}^{2}y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{x}^{2}y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & ={e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+({x}^{2}+1)y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & ={e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+({x}^{2}+1)y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}) & ={e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+({x}^{2}+1)y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+({x}^{2}+1)y}{1-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-334602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+(x+1)y}{1-2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+({x}^{2}+1)y}{1-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+({x}^{2}+1)y}{2-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{x}^{2}y}{1-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{2x}-{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+({x}^{2}+1)y}{1-{x}_{\\text{new}}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{{e}^{2x}+{e}^{2{x}_{\\text{new}}}+({x}^{2}+1)y}{1-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4x-5y,\\,y(-2)=1\n$$\n\nThe trapezoidal method is applied with step size $Δx=5.$ Find the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the current values $x$ and $y,$ and the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4x-5y+(4{x}_{\\text{new}}-5{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(4x+4{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y)-\\frac{25}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{5}{2}(4x+4{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y)-\\frac{25}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{5}{2}\\,(4x+4{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{23}{5}y)-\\frac{25}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{27}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{5}{2}\\,(4x+4{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{23}{5}y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{5}{27}\\,(4x+4{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{23}{5}y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{27}(20x+20{x}_{\\text{new}}-23y)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-334596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{1}{27}(19x+20{x}_{\\text{new}}-23y)"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{1}{27}(20x+19{x}_{\\text{new}}-23y)"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{1}{27}(20x+20{x}_{\\text{new}}-21y)"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{1}{27}(20x+20{x}_{\\text{new}}-22y)"] ["math" "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{1}{27}(20x+20{x}_{\\text{new}}-23y)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-334596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{1}{27}(20x+20{x}_{\\text{new}}-23y)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y({x}^{2}+1),\\,y(-1)=\\frac{11}{3}\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step to approximate $y\\,(-\\frac{1}{2}),$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\ny\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})≈{{field-1}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=-\\frac{1}{2}-(-1)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(y({x}^{2}+1)+{y}_{\\text{new}}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1))\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}y({x}^{2}+1)+\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{4}y({x}^{2}+1)+\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{4}y({x}^{2}+5)+\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}y({x}^{2}+5) \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(3-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{4}y({x}^{2}+5) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y({x}^{2}+5)}{3-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=-1+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y({x}^{2}+5)}{3-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{11}{3}((-1)^{2}+5)}{3-{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{22}{(\\frac{11}{4})} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})≈8.00.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-339764" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339764" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6.99"] ["math" "7.92"] ["math" "8.00"] ["math" "9.03"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339764" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8.00"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y(3\\sqrt{x}+2),\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step to approximate $y(1),$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\ny(1)≈{{field-1}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(y(3\\sqrt{x}+2)+{y}_{\\text{new}}(3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+2))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,y(3\\sqrt{x}+2)+\\frac{1}{2}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}(3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,y(3\\sqrt{x}+2)+\\frac{1}{2}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}(3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+2) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}y(3\\sqrt{x}+4)+\\frac{1}{2}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}(3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}(3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+2) & =\\frac{1}{2}y(3\\sqrt{x}+4) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}(-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}) & =\\frac{1}{2}y(3\\sqrt{x}+4) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y(3\\sqrt{x}+4)}{3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0+1=1.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y(3\\sqrt{x}+4)}{3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(3\\sqrt{0}+4)}{3\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & ≈-2.67.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈-2.67.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-339873" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339873" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1.43"] ["math" "-2.67"] ["math" "-2.76"] ["math" "-2.99"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339873" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2.67"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1),\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step to approximate $y(2),$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\ny(2)≈{{field-1}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)+{y}_{\\text{new}}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}})+1))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}})+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}})+1) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+3)+\\frac{1}{2}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}})+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}})+1) & =\\frac{1}{2}y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+3) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}(1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}})) & =\\frac{1}{2}y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+3) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+3)}{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=1+1=2.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+3)}{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{\\text{new}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+3)}{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\  & ≈-7.77.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈-7.77.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-339628" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339628" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6.34"] ["math" "-7.77"] ["math" "3.11"] ["math" "6.24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339628" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7.77"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4x-3y,\\,y(-1)=1\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step to approximate $y\\,(-\\frac{1}{3}),$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\ny\\,(-\\frac{1}{3})≈{{field-1}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=-\\frac{1}{3},$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=-\\frac{1}{3}-(-1)=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4x-3y+(4{x}_{\\text{new}}-3{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(4x-3y+4{x}_{\\text{new}}-3{y}_{\\text{new}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(4x+4{x}_{\\text{new}}-3y)-{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{3}(4x+4{x}_{\\text{new}}-3y)-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{3}(4x+4{x}_{\\text{new}})-{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{4}{3}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2}{3}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=-1+\\frac{2}{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2}{3}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(-1+(-\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & ≈-0.89.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y\\,(-\\frac{1}{3})≈-0.89.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-339758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.50"] ["math" "-0.89"] ["math" "-1.11"] ["math" "-1.20"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.89"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-x+4y,\\,y(1)=0\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step to approximate $y(3),$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\ny(3)≈{{field-1}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=3,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=3-1=2.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x+4y+(-{x}_{\\text{new}}+4{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+4y+4{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+4y+4{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+5y+4{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{y}_{\\text{new}} & =-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+5y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{3}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=1+2=3.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{3}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(1+3-5\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & ≈1.33.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(3)≈1.33.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-339748" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339748" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.21"] ["math" "1.25"] ["math" "1.33"] ["math" "1.53"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339748" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.33"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339856" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x-3y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with two steps to approximate $y(1)$ and $y(2),$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\ny(1)≈{{field-1}},\\,y(2)≈{{field-2}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339856" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(2).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=2$ is $2,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-0}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((2x-3y)+(2{x}_{\\text{new}}-3{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-3y)-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-3y)-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y)-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{5}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(1)$ and $y(2).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{5}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=1,\\,y=0.20.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{5}(2x+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2-0.20) \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{25} \\\\  & =1.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny(1)≈0.20,\\,y(2)≈1.16.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339856" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0dd15e47a99a1bb9ded57fdf081c20fef121aa27bf96de70b9ca6973e1f38b92"} {"question" "q-339856" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9dcac74f571889b1efd0"} {"question" "q-339856" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.21"] ["math" "0.20"] ["math" "0.89"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json" "file_sha256" "b96a57c5f8f6e3aaee3877a2d45be8f978e12e7e10cf9d